---
title: Buffalo Chicken Dip
description: A creamy, cheesy baked dip loaded with shredded chicken, ranch, and hot sauce that's perfect for game day and parties.
course: appetizer
cuisine: American
servings: 12
time required: 45 minutes
prep time: 10 minutes
cook time: 35 minutes
source: https://theforkedspoon.com/buffalo-chicken-dip-recipe/
image: https://theforkedspoon.com/wp-content/uploads/2018/12/Buffalo-Chicken-Dip-4.jpg
tags: [appetizer, dip, chicken, buffalo]
---

Bring a #large pot{} of water to a boil, add @boneless skinless chicken breasts{3%large}, and return to a boil. Remove from the heat, cover with a tight lid, and poach ~chicken{25%minutes}. Rest, then shred.

Preheat the #oven{} to 350F and spray a #9x9-inch baking pan{} with non-stick cooking spray.

In a #medium saucepot{} over medium-low heat, whisk together @cream cheese{8%oz}(cubed), @ranch dressing{1%cup}, @hot sauce{1%cup}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, and @garlic powder{1%tsp} until melted and creamy. Remove from the heat.

Stir in the shredded chicken, @green onion{1/2%cup}(chopped), @mozzarella cheese{1%cup}(shredded), and @cheddar cheese{1%cup}(shredded).

Transfer the mixture to the baking pan and top with the remaining @mozzarella cheese{1/2%cup}(shredded) and @cheddar cheese{1/2%cup}(shredded).

Bake ~oven{20-30%minutes} until melted and bubbling. Switch the oven to broil and cook ~broil{2-3%minutes} until golden brown, then remove immediately.

Serve with @tortilla chips{} or @vegetable sticks{}.
